Differences in variance aren't surprising here (because most of the
survey questions I encoded to 1-6, but there's one probability
question which takes the range 0-100), so I figured I should check
that that wasn't related, although I didn't see how higher variances
could possibly missing values/NAs like the errors complained about,
since lavaan hadn't had any problem with both models and blavaan had
fit the first model without any trouble:

    R> b2 <- bsem(model2, n.chains=6,
jagcontrol=list(method="rjparallel"), fixed.x=FALSE, sample=500,
