You are right that the PPC code could be better optimized.

Regarding the crash, my initial thought was that the default prior distributions didn't make sense when we have variables with large variances. But, in this case, it seems that we crash in a call to lavaan that attempts to calculate a log-likelihood. If you fit the same model in lavaan and try

fitMeasures(fit)

you will see that logl is NA. I'm not immediately sure why this happens, but I would generally recommend scaling the variables to have smaller variances.

Ed

